Now, let's create the `generateMD5Hash` method as follows:

```java
import java.math.BigInteger;
import java.nio.charSet.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class HashUtil {
    private static final Map<String, byte[]> cache = new HashMap<>();

    public static byte[] generateMD5Hash(String... strings) {
        String concatenatedStr = concatStringsEfficiently(strings);
        return calculateMD5Hash(concatenatedStr);
    }

    private static String concatStringsEfficiently(String... strings) {
        StringBuilder buffer = new StringBuilder();
        Map<String, Integer> stringLengths = new HashMap<>();

        for (String str : strings) {
            if (!stringLengths.containsKey(str)) {
                stringLengths.put(str, str.length());
            }
            buffer.append(str);

            if (buffer.length() > MAX_CONCATENATED_LENGTH) {
                int trimIndex = Math.max(0, buffer.length() - MAX_CONCATENATED_LENGTH);
                buffer.delete(trimIndex, buffer.length());
            }
        }

        // Remove leading and trailing whitespaces, reduce consecutive spaces to a single space
        buffer.replaceAll("\\s+", " ");
        buffer = new StringBuilder(buffer.toString().trim());
        return buffer.toString();
    }

    private static byte[] calculateMD5Hash(String input) {
        try {
            MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");
            byte[] messageDigest = md.digest(input.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
            return Arrays.copyOf(messageDigest, messageDigest.length);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            throw new RuntimeException(e);
        }
    }
}
```

Note that the constant `MAX_CONCATENATED_LENGTH` should be defined at the top of your source file or in a configuration property, depending on your application requirements. You can adjust this value according to your performance and memory usage needs.

