The function takes care of not exceeding the maximum allowed number of structures (M) and ensures that each structure has a unique RNTI value and RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG. If the number of structures exceeds M, it drops the oldest structure to make space for new ones. The code also manages memory efficiently by reusing allocated memory when possible.

The function generates random CRCFLAG values using `rand() % 2 == 0 ? true : false`. The RNTI values are generated within a reasonable range of [1, 10000) to ensure uniqueness and efficiency in comparison operations.']

